   "evidence": "Line 87 `let _ : Flat (I.subscheme\u03b9 \u226b f) := hI.flat` is the only occurrence of `hI` in the proof of `flat_relativeBaseChange`; lines 98-99 show `relativeBaseChange_iff` uses `hI` only via `hI.flat_relativeBaseChange g`. The conclusion `Flat (pullback.snd (I.subscheme\u03b9 \u226b f) g)` follows from `AlgebraicGeometry.Flat.isStableUnderBaseChange` (mathlib/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/Morphisms/Flat.lean:79,87) with no reference to the effective Cartier condition.",
   "file": "TauCeti/AlgebraicGeometry/EffectiveCartierDivisor/Relative.lean",
   "fix": "Replace the hypothesis in both by `(h : Flat (I.subscheme\u03b9 \u226b f))` (moving them out of the `IsRelativeEffectiveCartier` namespace, e.g. `flat_comap_of_flat` / `isRelativeEffectiveCartier_comap_iff`), and keep `IsRelativeEffectiveCartier.flat_relativeBaseChange` only if a dot-notation form is wanted, derived from the general lemma.",
   "issue": "`flat_relativeBaseChange` takes `hI : I.IsRelativeEffectiveCartier f` but uses only `hI.flat` (line 87 is the sole use), so the effective-Cartier half is an unused hypothesis that narrows the lemma. The file's Main results entry (line 29) advertises the general claim \"relative flatness is preserved by arbitrary base change\", which is true for any `I` with `Flat (I.subscheme\u03b9 \u226b f)` and does not hold only for effective Cartier divisors. Same defect at line 93: `relativeBaseChange_iff` needs only `Flat (I.subscheme\u03b9 \u226b f)` \u2014 its `mp` direction is a projection using no hypothesis, and its `mpr` goes through `flat_relativeBaseChange`.",
   "line": "84"
  }
